# Synthetic official-wire OTLP examples, not real .NET/Next.js exporter qualification.
# Generate with task demo:diagnostics (or diagnostics-generate with local.env exported).
# Send in order. Exact files retain IDs/times for replay; generation creates a new tag.

### Owner login
# @expect 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

< ./generated/diagnostics-login.json

### .NET-like Error-status span and exception event using standard OTLP protobuf
# @expect 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/traces
Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
Authorization: Bearer {{serverToken}}

< ./generated/diagnostics-traces.bin

### Next-like exception and custom error body, including one error without session context
# @expect 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/logs
Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
Authorization: Bearer {{serverToken}}

< ./generated/diagnostics-logs.bin

### App-wide error discovery does not require selecting an anonymous visit
# @expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/errors?q={{diagnosticsTag}}

### Identical span replay retains exact trace/span identity
# @expect 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/traces
Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
Authorization: Bearer {{serverToken}}

< ./generated/diagnostics-traces.bin

### Identical log replay retains exact event IDs
# @expect 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/logs
Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
Authorization: Bearer {{serverToken}}

< ./generated/diagnostics-logs.bin

### Same protected read after replay: record counts and identities must remain stable
# @expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/errors?q={{diagnosticsTag}}
